 "notes": "1927 three-storey flats. Pale butter-cream stucco, rusticated cream block street storey, two box bays across both upper storeys with dark frames; a full-width dark teal glazed-tile frieze under a moulded cap; ground (viewer's left to right): deep dark entry behind an iron gate, wide shop window behind a grille, narrow dark grilled door. Whiter upper wall over the cream rusticated street storey (block joints on the piers), royal-blue grille on the wide centre opening, wide dark entry door at the left, teal coping deepened to project past the bay caps so it reads continuous. Butter-cream #eeebd2, bays two-light single mullion with dark frames, bright blue #1e4fa8 grille, dentil row under the teal band. Bay centre faces read as one large undivided pane (lightM 1.4); mirror claim skipped again. Staggered vertical block joints on the ground piers (square ashlar), darker green frieze #27504b. Scallop frieze not expressible. Tint lift (2026-10-02): wall tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k).",
